=== PIPELINE_STATE head
# Pipeline state

Computed by `tools/pipeline_state.py` from the filesystem and the scheduler. Nothing here is
maintained by hand, because a hand-maintained record is how this project lost its best model.

Run it again at any time:

```
ssh go2432@grid.wayne.edu
~/mambaforge/envs/spineps/bin/python ~/spinesurg-ct-nnunet/tools/pipeline_state.py
```

| stage | status | group | what | proof it finished |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `bank_v3` | READY | data | Merge the oblique renders and VinDr into allspine_v3 | `rung_1.npz` |
| `bank_v5` | READY | data | Build allspine_v5 with every pseudo-labelled real radiograph | `rung_1.npz` |
| `data_fixes` | READY | data | Film-match measurement, anchored-only pseudolabel filter, film-matched render bank (v2fm) | `film_match_measure.json` |
| `hires_refetch` | READY | data | Refetch publisher originals for the low-resolution literature panels | `hires_report.json` |
| `repro_feasibility` | READY | deliverable | One job that recomputes every manuscript number from raw inputs and writes a hashed ledger | `LEDGER.tsv` |
| `seed_sweep` | READY | eval | Multi-seed spread of the run-level head | `*.json` |
| `sweep_fix` | READY | eval | Three fixes found on the 25 held-out real films: a detector box on a real vertebra the annotation does not cover is 'unlabelled', not a false positive; chain nodes are placed by panorama position and merged when they coincide; --hybrid local compares the count and the variant alphabet only on the bodies they name differently | `sweep.json` |
| `bank_v4` | blocked | data | Add AASCE to make allspine_v4 | `rung_1.npz` |
| `competitor_train` | done | benchmark | Re-implement the published registration-free paradigms and train them on the newest bank | `*_val.npz` |
| `ensemble_eval` | done | benchmark | Ask whether any COMBINATION of those methods beats the best single one, with and without the map | `ensemble.json` |
| `aasce_convert` | done | data | Convert the AASCE radiographs to the render format | `*.json` |
| `aasce_crops` | done | data | Cut AASCE into context crops | `rung_1.npz` |
| `anomaly_manifest` | done | data | Every anomalous spine we hold, in three tiers by how far the label can be trusted | `spine_classes.json` |
| `buu_correct` | done | data | Promote BUU's S1a line to L6 on six-lumbar studies; flag L5 sacralised on four-lumbar; review package | `CORRECTION_SUMMARY.json` |
| `disk_cleanup` | done | data | Bring the home directory back under the 4 TB quota | `disk_cleanup_manifest.txt` |
| `lat236_pseudo` | done | data | Label the 236 IEEE whole-spine laterals | `pseudolabel_report.json` |
| `mendeley_crops` | done | data | Cut the Mendeley lateral films into context crops | `rung_1.npz` |
| `nhanes_pseudo` | done | data | Label the 16,530 unannotated NHANES films | `pseudolabel_report.json` |
| `pseudo_gate` | done | data | Score the pseudo-labeller against the 543 human-annotated NHANES films | `pseudolabel_report.json` |
| `source_quality` | done | data | Every bank source with its label origin and crop quality | `source_quality.json` |
| `ts_drr` | done | data | TotalSegmentator v2.0.1 (1228 clinical CTs under ~/data/TotalSegmentator) rendered to lateral DRRs with per-vertebra boxes -> ~/ts_drr, the ann/img layout every sweep tool reads | `*.json` |
| `vindr_pseudo` | done | data | Label the 9,722 unused VinDr-SpineXR films | `pseudolabel_report.json` |
| `product_select` | done | deliverable | Rank every encoder by twin-free ordinary interior accuracy; model cards; private checkpoint publishing | `PRODUCT_RANKING.json` |
| `review_pack` | done | deliverable | Pack the pseudolabelled films students review, and deploy the private review Space | `manifest.json` |
| `corpus_levels` | done | doc | Per-level counts across the expanded corpus, split by how each label was obtained | `CORPUS_LEVELS.md` |
| `dataset_usage` | done | doc | Which X-ray datasets reach a bank and why the rest do not | `XRAY_DATASET_USAGE.md` |
| `morning_brief` | done | doc | The overnight brief | `MORNING_BRIEF_2026-09-16.md` |
| `student_pack` | done | doc | The worklist, renderings and guide for students to correct fluoroscopy labels | `*.csv` |
| `anchor_free` | done | eval | Accuracy on windows that contain no landmark at all | `*_head.json` |
| `anomaly_cooc` | done | eval | Recount both border anomalies from the label voxels and test co-occurrence | `anomaly_cooccurrence_labels.json` |
| `benchmark_cina` | done | eval | Every pairing, and every external method with predictions, under Cina 2021's task definition on the same public films | `benchmark_cina.json` |
| `eval_flags` | done | eval | Operating points for the rule flags against known transitional cases | `flags_r18_ce_v2.json` |
| `eval_head_transitional` | done | eval | Transitional strata with the head on and off | `transitional_eval_*.json` |
| `eval_rawfilms` | done | eval | Every arm on one held-out set, split into real film and render | `rawfilms_*.json` |
| `explain` | done | eval | Region-occlusion ablation, Grad-CAM, embedding geometry, prototypes, morphometric probes | `explain.json` |
| `feasibility_claims` | done | eval | The feasibility report's claims C1-C5, each with a number, on anomalous AND ordinary spines | `feasibility_claims.json` |
| `fov_separability` | done | eval | Field of view against separability of the four spine classes, and the threshold | `fov_separability.json` |
| `geometric_indices` | done | eval | The feasibility report's own recommended detectors, scored on real film with real ground truth | `geometric_indices_buu.json` |
| `global_signature` | done | eval | Does a vertebra far from both junctions know its spine is anomalous | `global_signature.json` |
| `interior_windows` | done | eval | Naming on windows whose PIXELS contain no anchor, film-clustered CIs, structural baselines | `interior_windows.json` |
| `panel_diagnosis` | done | eval | Why the literature panels score 19.7% against 95.1% on real film | `panel_vs_film_stats.json` |
| `push99` | done | eval | Logit-adjusted training for the rare alphabet classes, and paired AP + lateral fusion | `interior_windows.json` |
| `role_head` | done | eval | The transition-role head, and the sweep arms that use it | `role_head_v3.pt` |
| `surgeon_benefit` | done | eval | Would the alert help a surgeon who counts from a landmark, or disturb one already right | `*.json` |
| `sweep_answers` | done | eval | The two analyses the result is quoted from: accuracy at a stated coverage, and per vertebra per spine class | `COVERAGE.json` |
| `sweep_improve` | done | eval | Three linker/placement improvements -- a global solve over consecutive and skip links, a phase-correlation seed, ECC refinement of the query placement -- each alone and together, against the fixed-step protocol baseline | `sweep.json` |
